Derived from Scratch (AGPL-3.0-only)
------------------------------------

Parts of this program are translations of, or are closely modelled on, code in
scratch-vm 5.0.300 and scratch-render 2.x by the Scratch Foundation
(https://github.com/scratchfoundation), licensed AGPL-3.0-only. They were
translated from JavaScript to C and Python and adapted in 2026. In particular:

  runtime/sched.c    thread scheduling, hats, clones, stop-all:
                     src/engine/sequencer.js, runtime.js, thread.js,
                     src/sprites/rendered-target.js
  runtime/value.c    Scratch casts and comparisons: src/util/cast.js,
  runtime/cg.c       src/blocks/scratch3_operators.js
  runtime/list.c     list blocks: src/blocks/scratch3_data.js
  runtime/blocks.c   looks, motion, sensing, pen and music blocks:
                     src/blocks/scratch3_looks.js, scratch3_motion.js,
                     scratch3_sensing.js, scratch3_sound.js,
                     src/extensions/scratch3_pen, scratch3_music,
                     src/util/color.js, math-util.js; sprite fencing from
                     scratch-render src/RenderWebGL.js
  ref/run.js,        stub renderer mirroring scratch-render's fencing and
  ref/stub-renderer.js  bounds behaviour
  scc/load.py        project.json interpretation mirroring scratch-vm's
                     deserialisation and block execution rules

The test oracle and benchmarks (ref/) run scratch-vm itself. It is downloaded
by bench/setup.sh and is not included in this repository. The benchmarks can
also download TurboWarp's scratch-vm fork (MPL-2.0), which is likewise not
included.


